  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The first term of an arithmetic series is ${a}_{1}=9$, the common difference is $d=8$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=636.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the number of terms, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d).\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${a}_{1}=9$, $d=8$ and ${S}_{N}=636$ into the above and solve for $N$, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 636 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 9+(N-1)\\cdot 8) \\\\ 636 & =\\frac{N}{2}(18+8N-8) \\\\ 636 & =\\frac{N}{2}(8N+10) \\\\ 636 & =N(4N+5) \\\\ 636 & =4{N}^{2}+5N \\\\ 4{N}^{2}+5N-636 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}-4\\cdot 4\\cdot (-636)}}{2\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{10\\,201}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 101}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=12$ or $N=-\\frac{106}{8}.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=12$ terms.",
